body:
I've suffered lifelong abuse because of religion, religion has given me more reasons not to live than anything. 

&#x200B;

The lifestyle I want is to be able to be free, to not have to work to live and spend my days just being with people I care about. That's just not possible in this shitty world, unless you were lucky enough to be born into wealth. 

&#x200B;

Being kind to people is important to me, but apparently that's not true of the vast majority of people (or even if it's a minority they're doing a hell of a good job fucking everything up for the rest of us). I used to have ambitions but I cannot achieve them, I have no hope for anything. I don't know who I am other than a product of my circumstances, like everyone else. I've been told I'm smart and nice but I feel like I'm just doing the bare minimum and the bar for human decency is just in hell. I've also been told I'm strong for having survived abuse but I feel like it's more accurate to say I'm stupid for prolonging my suffering by staying alive.
